  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the file set for the listener-container threading refactor across all three repos, ordered most important first:\n\n**spring-kafka (primary implementation)** \u2014 `ConcurrentMessageListenerContainer.java`, `KafkaMessageListenerContainer.java`, `AbstractMessageListenerContainer.java`, `MessageListenerContainer.java` (interface), `ContainerProperties.java`, `ConcurrentKafkaListenerContainerFactory.java`, `AbstractKafkaListenerContainerFactory.java`, `KafkaListenerEndpoint.java`, `AbstractKafkaListenerEndpoint.java`, `KafkaListenerAnnotationBeanPostProcessor.java`, `EnableKafka.java`, plus the three related test classes.\n\n**spring-boot (autoconfiguration consumer)** \u2014 `KafkaAutoConfiguration.java`, `KafkaAnnotationDrivenConfiguration.java`, `KafkaProperties.java`, `ConcurrentKafkaListenerContainerFactoryConfigurer.java`, plus their test counterparts.\n\n**spring-framework (core abstractions)** \u2014 `TaskExecutor.java` and `AsyncTaskExecutor.java`, the concurrency abstractions the container's per-consumer execution model builds on (`MessageListenerContainer` extends `SmartLifecycle`; concurrency execution flows through Spring's `TaskExecutor` hierarchy).\n\nAlso included the two asciidoc references (`kafka.adoc`, `changes-since-1.0.adoc`) since they document the existing `setConcurrency`/`ConcurrentKafkaListenerContainerFactory` contract and prior breaking-change precedent, both directly relevant to drafting the breaking-vs-compatible annotations in the plan.",
